<header><p class="st-kicker">chiefdom · Central and Southern Africa</p><h1 class="st-title">Herero Paramountcy</h1><p class="st-meta">1863 CE – 1904 CE (approx.) · capital Okahandja</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The cattle-rich Herero chieftaincy of Okahandja, whose 1904 rising against German rule ended in genocide.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/herero-people">Herero</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bantu-peoples">Bantu-speaking</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cattle">cattle</a> herders of central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/namibia">Namibia</a>, had been raided for decades by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jonker-afrikaner">Jonker Afrikaner's</a> <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/orlam-afrikaner-state">Orlam Afrikaner State</a>. In 1863 they rose under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maharero">Kamaherero</a>, known as Maharero, at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/otjimbingwe">Otjimbingwe</a> and won their independence, confirmed by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peace-of-okahandja">Peace of Okahandja</a> in 1870.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maharero">Maharero</a> made <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/okahandja">Okahandja</a> the seat of a paramountcy over many <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/herero-people">Herero</a> chiefs, though authority was shared with lineage heads. Wealth lay in vast herds, and the holy fire of each homestead linked the living with ancestors. Rhenish missionaries were active, and in 1885 Maharero signed a protection treaty with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/samuel-maharero">Samuel Maharero</a> succeeded him in 1890.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Land loss, debt and abuses under <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/german-south-west-africa">German South West Africa</a> led to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/herero-people">Herero</a> rising in January 1904. After the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-waterberg">battle of Waterberg</a>, General <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lothar-von-trotha">von Trotha</a> ordered their extermination; most Herero died in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/omaheke">Omaheke</a> desert or in camps.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="chiefdom, 1863 CE – 1904 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><ellipse cx="44" cy="56" rx="16" ry="24"/><path d="M44 34 V78"/><path d="M68 20 V84"/><path d="M68 20 L63 30 H73 Z"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">chiefdom</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Central and Southern Africa</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:96.78%;width:1.20%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1863 CE – 1904 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>chiefdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Okahandja</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Maharero, Samuel Maharero</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Herero traditional religion, Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Otjiherero</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/namibia">Namibia</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Herero chieftaincy of Okahandja, Ovaherero</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1884&amp;focus=herero-paramountcy" aria-label="Herero Paramountcy on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5134 2990 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Herero Paramountcy lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5454 3246L5457 3267M5454 3246L5457 3267"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5457 3267h0M5457 3267h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5454 3246h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5454 3246h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Okahandja. <a href="/atlas?year=1884&amp;focus=herero-paramountcy">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
